---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, u } from '../lib/site';
const c = site.company;
const a = site.analytics?.provider && site.analytics?.id ? site.analytics.provider : '';
---
<Legal title="Privacy notice | Stefano Di Rico" h1="Privacy notice" path="/privacy/" updated="13 November 2026"
  description="How di-rico.com handles personal data: no contact forms, no tracking cookies by default, and who to contact about your data.">
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>This website is run by {c.name}, a company registered in {c.registeredIn} (company number {c.number}), registered office {c.office}. It is the data controller for this site. For anything about your data, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Privacy`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
  <h3>When you email us</h3>
  <p>There are no forms on this site. If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to write. We use it only to reply and to arrange what you asked about, such as a booking or a media request. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests (answering enquiries) or, for a booking, taking steps to enter into a contract. Email is provided by Google Workspace. We keep enquiries for up to two years after the last message, and booking records for six years for accounting purposes.</p>
  <h3>When you visit</h3>
  <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like every web host, GitHub receives your IP address and basic browser details in order to deliver the pages, and keeps server logs for security. We do not have access to those logs. GitHub is based in the United States and transfers data under the UK and EU data protection frameworks. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>
  <p>Fonts and images are served from this site itself, not from Google Fonts or another third party.</p>
  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  {a === 'goatcounter' && <p>We count visits with GoatCounter, which uses no cookies and stores no personal data: no IP addresses, and nothing that follows you between sites. It tells us which pages are read and roughly where visitors come from. You can object at any time by emailing us or by using a browser content blocker.</p>}
  {a === 'ga4' && <p>If, and only if, you accept analytics cookies, we use Google Analytics 4 to count visits. Google sets cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) and processes usage data, including a shortened IP address, on our behalf. Our lawful basis is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time through “Cookie settings” in the footer.</p>}
  {!a && <p>We do not use any analytics on this site.</p>}
  <h3>Podcast audio and embedded players</h3>
  <p>Podcast audio is hosted by Spotify for Creators. When you press play on an episode, your browser requests the audio file from Spotify, which receives your IP address and counts the download. Nothing is requested until you press play.</p>
  <p>Spotify and YouTube players are switched off until you allow “embedded media”. If you allow them, those companies set their own cookies and may record what you play. See the <a href={u('/cookies')}>cookie policy</a>.</p>
  <h3>Links to other sites</h3>
  <p>We link to LinkedIn, Instagram, TikTok, Substack, Spotify, Apple Podcasts and YouTube. They have their own privacy policies, and nothing is shared with them until you follow a link.</p>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell personal data or use it for advertising. It is handled only by the suppliers named above (GitHub for hosting, Google Workspace for email, Spotify for podcast audio{a === 'goatcounter' ? ', GoatCounter for visit counts' : ''}{a === 'ga4' ? ', Google Analytics if you consent' : ''}), and by professional advisers or authorities where the law requires it.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK GDPR and EU GDPR you can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, object to or restrict how we use it, and withdraw consent. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Privacy`}>{site.email}</a> and we will reply within one month.</p>
  <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, please tell us first. You can also complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a> in the UK, or to your local data protection authority in the EU.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is suitable for all ages and does not knowingly collect data from children. If you are under 18, please ask a parent, carer or teacher before emailing us.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this notice changes, the new version will be published here with a new date.</p>
</Legal>
